{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevPeakValue","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.KashaevPeakValue","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevAsymptotic","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolumeSaddle","lean:module:QOU.Knot.LobTaylorSaddle"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaevProd_saddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaevProd_saddle","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevPeakValue.lean#L82-L173","doc":"**At the saddle.**  For `k` within one step of `5N/6` — which `⌊5N/6⌋` is —\nthe expansion above can be re-centred on the exact saddle angle `5π/6`, paying\n`O(1/N)` for the offset.\n\nThe hypothesis is stated as a bound on `|θ_k − 5π/6|` rather than as\n`k = ⌊5N/6⌋`, because that is what the proof uses and because both `⌊5N/6⌋`\nand `⌈5N/6⌉` satisfy it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaevProd_asymptotic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaevProd_asymptotic","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevPeakValue.lean#L44-L80","doc":"**The join.**  `log(kashaevProd N k)` is twice the log-sine sum, so the\nEuler–Maclaurin expansion of the latter doubles into an expansion of the\nformer — with the same `O(1/N²)` error, doubled.\n\nThis is the first statement in the development that expands the Kashaev term\nitself rather than a ratio of Kashaev terms. ","signatureChunk":0}]}